# Git / Jira / PR workflow

## Before starting work

1. If the user has not given a **Jira ticket key** (e.g. `KAN-12`), **ask for it** before coding, branching, or committing feature work.
2. If the ticket is already known from the message, links, or prior context, use it — do not ask again.
3. Prefer one ticket per branch.

## Branch naming

Create a branch from the latest `main` (or the agreed base) using:

| Prefix | Use when |
| --- | --- |
| `feat/` | New feature or capability |
| `fix/` | Correcting broken or incorrect behavior |
| `bugfix/` | Explicit bug ticket / defect fix |

**Format:** `{prefix}/{jira-key}-{short-kebab-title}`

Examples:

- `feat/KAN-9-project-knowledge-docs`
- `fix/KAN-12-status-panel-error-state`
- `bugfix/KAN-15-history-table-crash`

Rules:

- Lowercase kebab-case for the title segment.
- Include the Jira key in the branch name.
- Keep the title short (roughly 3–6 words).
- Do not use spaces, underscores, or vague names like `feat/updates`.

## Commit, push, and PR

1. Commit on the feature branch (only when the user asks to commit, or when they ask to push/PR and a commit is required first).
2. When the user asks to **push**, push the branch and **open a pull request** (do not push straight to `main` for ticket work).
3. PR title should mirror the work and include the ticket, e.g. `feat(KAN-9): add project knowledge docs` or `[KAN-9] Add project knowledge docs`.
4. **PR body is mandatory** and must include all three sections below (plus a Jira link when available). Use Mermaid for the diagram when possible.
5. Never force-push to `main`/`master`.

### Required PR body sections

Every PR description **must** contain these sections in order:

#### 1. High-level diagram

A Mermaid (or ASCII) diagram of the change: request/flow, main modules touched, or before→after. Keep it readable in GitHub.

#### 2. Description

What changed and why (scope in/out, key behavior, risks). Link the Jira ticket.

#### 3. Test cases

Concrete cases (IDs from the ticket when present) as a checklist or table: given / when / then, plus commands like `npm test` when relevant.

**Template (required headings):**

1. `## High-level diagram` — Mermaid `flowchart` (or clear ASCII) of the change
2. `## Description` — what/why, scope, Jira link
3. `## Test cases` — checklist or table (ticket TC-IDs when present) plus `npm test` / manual checks

Repo template: [`.github/pull_request_template.md`](../../.github/pull_request_template.md).

## Quick checklist

- [ ] Jira key known (asked if missing)
- [ ] Branch named `feat|fix|bugfix/{KEY}-{title}`
- [ ] Push goes to that branch
- [ ] PR created after push
- [ ] PR body has **diagram**, **description**, and **test cases**
